; FM3 unison: in special mode each operator of CH3 takes its own pitch, so
; one channel can be a four-voice unison. The same line twice: first all
; four operators on one pitch (a plain voice), then spread -60, -20, +20
; and +60 cents (one thick, beating voice).
(def-fm pad4 init-fm :alg 7 :fb 0
  :ar1 20 :ar2 20 :ar3 20 :ar4 20
  :tl1 14 :tl2 14 :tl3 14 :tl4 14
  :rr1 6 :rr2 6 :rr3 6 :rr4 6
)

(def line :len 4 c e g > c < b g e d c1)

(fm3 pad4)
(fm3-1 line :pitch -60 line)
(fm3-2 line :pitch -20 line)
(fm3-3 line :pitch 20 line)
(fm3-4 line :pitch 60 line)
